= Introduction

Present the problematic of this internship : numerical disturbances in compressible fluid simulation, and the carbuncle. get to why this internship is necessary, and what it will bring. then explain how we are going to get there.

This internship is focused on understanding numerical methods for hyperbolic systems of equations.
A first objective is to implement the finite volume method with different Riemann solvers for the Euler equations.
Afterwards, we will implement a test suite that triggers grid-aligned numerical instabilities for the AeroSol software @AeroSol.
Finally these tests are going to be used on a curl and divergence preserving method develloped by the team at Cagire.

Cagire is a team of Inria Bordeaux working on various high performance flow simulations. These flow include complex physical properties like being multiphasic, turbulent and multiscale. They also work on efficient high order numerical methods for complex geometries.

